# Otharri's "{2}{R}{W}, Tap an untapped Rebel you control: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped"
# chooses its Rebel as the cost is paid, once the mana abilities have been activated (CR 601.2g-h by way of 602.2b). On
# turn 11 Bot1's only Rebel is the token Otharri's attack made on turn 9. Bot1 pays the {W} with Springleaf Drum, which
# taps that Rebel for its own cost, and the rest with three Mountains: no untapped Rebel is left to tap for Otharri's cost
# - a tapped permanent can't be tapped to pay a cost (CR 118.3) - so it can't be paid, and the activation is taken back
# (CR 733.1): Otharri stays in the graveyard, the Drum, the Rebel and the Mountains untapped, the pool empty. Then Bot1
# pays with a Plains instead of the Drum, taps the Rebel for the cost, and Otharri returns tapped.

